# Repository engineering contracts

Use this file for local exceptions and requirements. Put always-applicable project
rules in AGENTS.md. Portable workflows come from the packaged Wai skills when Wai
is installed: wai-api-contracts, wai-testing, wai-safe-refactor, wai-delivery, and the
confirmed stack skill. Load only the workflows relevant to the task.

## Verified stack and commands

- Stack: {{stack}}; language: {{language}}.
- Tests: {{testCommand}}.
- Static/type checks: {{analyzeCommand}}.
- Required integration/device/database checks: <FILL ME — evidence: CI and existing tests>.

## Authoritative contracts

- Contract/schema/route source: <FILL ME — evidence: actual producer and consumer files>.
- Serialization/default/nullability requirements: <FILL ME — evidence: schemas and fixtures>.
- Error mapping and retry/idempotency policy: <FILL ME — evidence: boundary handlers and callers>.
- Authorization/ownership boundary: <FILL ME — evidence: effective middleware and service checks>.
- Sensitive data handling and prohibited logging: <FILL ME — evidence: project configuration>.
- Migration/compatibility requirements: <FILL ME — evidence: persisted shapes and supported clients>.

Inspect affected producers and consumers before selecting an implementation order.
Do not assume every project contains a BFF, both client and server, or the same token
storage policy. These placeholders are unconfirmed until replaced with source evidence.

## Preservation and completion

- Preserve: <FILL ME — evidence: explicit developer requirements and existing behavior>.
- Verify changed behavior with appropriate checks and meaningful negative-path tests.
- A partial change or an unchanged preservation invariant does not make a plan stale.
- Use one active plan. Check review-returned progress before done; a code pass can leave
  the step incomplete.
- Complete review must include intended new files and disclose missing evidence.
- Before an authorized Git/SVN commit, inspect exact contents and include intended new
  files without bulk-adding tool state, build output, or unrelated changes.
- Report executed checks, skipped/unverified criteria, review coverage, remaining
  findings, and commit status. Model approval is not execution evidence.

Authoritative project docs: <FILL ME — evidence: maintained repository documentation>.
